## kro Kubernetes RBAC

Separate from AWS IAM: kro needs Kubernetes RBAC to create the ACK custom resources while
reconciling the instance.

| Layer | Controls | Who needs it |
|---|---|---|
| AWS IAM | API calls to AWS | ACK controller role |
| Kubernetes RBAC | Access to CRDs/CRs in the cluster | kro controller role |

Without it, reconciliation fails with `... is forbidden: User "...-kro-capability/KRO" cannot get
resource ...`.

API groups used by this migration:

| API group | Resources |
|---|---|
{% for g in notes.api_groups %}| `{{ g.group }}` | {{ g.plurals|join(', ') }} |
{% endfor %}

{% if notes.managed_capability %}
Handled automatically by EKS Auto Mode managed capabilities. For self-managed kro, grant an EKS
access entry to the kro role or bind a ClusterRole scoped to the groups above.
{% else %}
Grant an EKS access entry for the kro role, or bind a ClusterRole scoped to the groups above.
{% endif %}

