## Rollback

Adoption is non-destructive and reversible:

- **`terraform.tfstate` is untouched.** Keep it as the rollback reference. Do not run
  `terraform destroy` — the AWS resources are now also described by ACK CRs.
- Every CR carries `services.k8s.aws/deletion-policy: retain`, so deleting a CR leaves the AWS
  resource intact.
- To roll back: delete the instance, then the RGD, then the CRs. The AWS resources survive and
  Terraform still describes them.
{% if notes.owner_references %}
- **`ownerReferences` ARE set on the adopted CRs.** Deleting the instance will cascade-delete the
  CRs. `deletion-policy: retain` still protects the AWS resources, but confirm that is the
  intent before applying.
{% else %}
- `ownerReferences` are deliberately omitted, so deleting the instance does not cascade into the
  CRs.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

